{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/makeIterator()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"makeIterator()","modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"makeIterator","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"Iterator","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V8IteratorV"}],"symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V12makeIteratorAC0D0Vyx_GyF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MaximalCliques.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques.swift#L273"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"makeIterator"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MaximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":">."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V8IteratorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Iterator"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/makeiterator()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence.makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"title":"Cliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","abstract":[],"role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/makeIterator()":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/makeIterator()","role":"symbol","title":"makeIterator()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/makeiterator()"